<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto III, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1261–1312</span> · Also known as Béla V of Hungary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto III was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a> from 1290, a Wittelsbach ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a>. As a grandson of King Béla IV through his mother, he was elected King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1305 as Béla V. He was captured by the Transylvanian voivode <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-kan">Ladislaus Kán</a> in 1307 and gave up his Hungarian claim, returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-iii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Otto III, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: János Thuróczy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_(Chronica_Hungarorum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
